# R essentials
Appendix A:

Download R for free from the Comprehensive R Archive Network (CRAN).
- R is an open-source free programming language focused on statistics
Download Rstudio, which is an Integrated Development Environment (IDE).
- Makes the language easier to understand
  - Ex. R is the engine and Rstudio is the car

Key concepts and skills; 
- Understand R and R studio and workflows
  - Ex. using dplr and making graphs with ggplot2 makes manipulating/understanding data
- Functionality of tidyverse
  - Ex. importing data, data manipulation, string manipulation
- Data science workflows
  - Ex. Class functions, data simulation

Software/packages needed: 
tidyverse is a collection of R packages designed for data science
- Base R
- Core tidyverse (including): *tidyverse is a package of packages*
  - dplyr (5 dplyr functions)
    - select(): picks a particular column
    - filter(): pick particular row of a dataset
          - Also dedicated function: slice()
    - arrange(): change the order of the dataset 
          - modify arrange() with (desc) to change ascending to descending 
          - modify arrange() with (accross) to arrange a variety of columns
    - mutate(): when we want to make a new column
          - could use mutate() with math, addition/subraction
          - could use mutate() with log(), lead(), lag(), cumsum()
          - could use mutate() with across()
    - summarise() or summarize(): when we would like to make new, condensed, summary variables
      - .by and count()
  - forcats
  - ggplot 2
  - readr
  - stringr
  - tibble
  - tidyr
- Outer tidyverse (must be loaded separate)
  - haven
  - lubridate
- janitor
*if you want to use a package, you first must install it and then load it when wanting to use*

# Install/load by:
install.packages()
library()
- install.packages(tidyverse)
- install.packages(janitor)
  - library(tidyverse)
  - library(lubridate)

Set up Posit Cloud
- Online version of Rstudio
- Each Posit Cloud workspace is esentially a new comp, must install packages each time

# Rstudio
Console: can type and execute Rcode line by line

naming:
my_name <- Ally
- Assignment operator allocates Ally to 'my_name'

Save the project with new rds file:
saveRDS(object = my_name, file = "my_first_file.rds")
